<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch-German trade stagnates in 1996.</title>
<headline>Dutch-German trade stagnates in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch-German trade levels were flat in 1996, despite a hefty increase in total German imports, the Dutch-German chamber of commerce said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said the value of total Dutch-German trade slipped by 0.4 percent to 115 billion marks (129 billion guilders).</p>
<p>Dutch exports to Germany fell one percent to 57.5 billion marks, while imports from Germany were steady at 57.3 billion.</p>
<p>The chamber said the stagnation in bilateral trade resulted from both countries having increasingly targeted fast-growing markets outside Europe, which have become more attractive due to the stronger dollar.</p>
